 34SI c  2010WaZT,2010Wa20: A 215-MeV {+36}S{+9+} beam was produced from the    
 34SI2c  XTU-Tandem ALPI-superconducting linear accelerator complex at the INFN 
 34SI3c  Legnaro National Laboratory, Italy. The target was 300-|mg/cm{+2}, 99.7%
 34SI4c  enriched {+208}Pb on a 20-|mg/cm{+2} carbon backing. Projectile-like   
 34SI5c  fragments produced in binary grazing reactions were separated and      
 34SI6c  identified by the PRISMA spectrometer. |g rays were detected using the 
 34SI7c  CLARA array of 22 escape-suppressed Ge clover detectors covering the   
 34SI8c  azimuthal angles from 98|' to 180|'. Measured E|g with Doppler         
 34SI9c  corrections, I|g, and ({+34}Si)|g-coin. Deduced levels. Compared with  
 34SIAc  shell-model calculations.                                              
